# Knowledge Transfer (KT): Standalone Code Quality Metrics Collector (KLOC & Defect Density)

===============================================================================
OBJECTIVE
===============================================================================

Design and implement a standalone utility that runs independently of the CI/CD
pipeline to collect code quality metrics from SonarQube and generate reports.

The utility will run from a dedicated Linux server (or VM) that has network
access to:

• SonarQube
• GitHub (optional)
• OpenShift (optional)
• Internal repositories

This utility is NOT part of the DevOps pipeline. It should be executable on
demand or via a scheduled cron job.

===============================================================================
GOAL
===============================================================================

Generate a quality report for each application containing:

• Project Name
• NCLOC (Non-Comment Lines of Code)
• KLOC
• Bugs
• Vulnerabilities
• Security Hotspots
• Code Smells
• Coverage
• Duplicated Code
• Reliability Rating
• Security Rating
• Maintainability Rating
• Defect Density
• Vulnerability Density
• Code Smell Density
• Scan Date
• Trend (optional)

Only first-party source code must be considered.

